  "facts": [
    "Opened 18 July 1934 by King George V, the Queensway Tunnel was the world’s longest road tunnel at 2.13 miles, a title it held until 1948 when Spain’s Vielha Tunnel surpassed it.",
    "In 1984, a £1 million lighting overhaul replaced outdated wall fixtures with modern overhead lights, using roof‑removed double‑decker buses as mobile work platforms, complete with toilets and catering.",
    "A 2004 safety upgrade added seven 21‑metre emergency refuges, each holding 180 people, equipped with fire‑resistant doors, wheelchair ramps, bottled water, toilets, and video links to the Mersey Tunnels Police."
